WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.324 --> 00:00:17.890
As Swallow watched the flock go, he felt a little sad.

2
00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:22.192
He'd been born into that flock.

3
00:00:23.332 --> 00:00:25.053
The other birds were his family.

4
00:00:27.034 --> 00:00:27.794
He'd miss them.

5
00:00:29.115 --> 00:00:32.356
Still, he knew in his heart he'd made the right choice.

6
00:00:33.796 --> 00:00:36.718
"I never want to leave my love again," he thought.

7
00:00:36.738 --> 00:00:42.142
"This perfect rose will show her I care."

8
00:00:46.205 --> 00:00:47.806
Swallow flew back to the lake.

9
00:00:49.207 --> 00:00:51.469
He swooped and dove over the water.

10
00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:55.512
He flew in fancy circles and loops.

11
00:00:58.294 --> 00:01:00.896
"I hope my reed is watching," he thought.

12
00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:05.282
"She'll see what a great and fast flyer I am!

13
00:01:06.622 --> 00:01:08.223
And she'll love this rose."

14
00:01:10.444 --> 00:01:14.267
Swallow came in for a landing as the sun was setting.

15
00:01:15.387 --> 00:01:16.448
But something was wrong.

16
00:01:17.688 --> 00:01:20.050
His beautiful reed had disappeared!

17
00:01:21.611 --> 00:01:25.373
In her place was a bent and wilted brown reed.

18
00:01:25.393 --> 00:01:29.835
"My most beautiful reed wilted!"

19
00:01:30.275 --> 00:01:31.016
Swallow thought.

20
00:01:32.048 --> 00:01:34.929
"This is the worst thing that has ever happened to me!"

21
00:01:37.371 --> 00:01:38.951
Swallow felt crushed.

22
00:01:40.212 --> 00:01:42.513
But then his situation got worse.

23
00:01:43.794 --> 00:01:46.155
A cold wind began to blow.

24
00:01:48.036 --> 00:01:49.396
Swallow shivered.

25
00:01:49.416 --> 00:01:52.278
"Brr! Leader was right.

26
00:01:53.438 --> 00:01:54.279
I'll freeze here.

27
00:01:55.419 --> 00:01:57.100
I need to find my flock right away."

28
00:01:59.636 --> 00:02:03.597
Swallow dropped the rose where his love stood wilting and took off.

29
00:02:05.298 --> 00:02:06.998
He flew as fast as he could.

30
00:02:07.838 --> 00:02:10.439
But the wind was sharp and strong.

31
00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:14.200
And he didn't see the flock anywhere.

32
00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:17.421
"I'll find them in the morning," he thought.

33
00:02:17.441 --> 00:02:20.902
"For now, I just need a warm place to sleep."

34
00:02:25.563 --> 00:02:27.184
Swallow looked around the town.

35
00:02:29.132 --> 00:02:30.433
"There's that beautiful statue.

36
00:02:33.135 --> 00:02:34.936
It's the perfect place to spend the night."

37
00:02:38.498 --> 00:02:41.360
Swallow landed between the statue's two feet.

38
00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:45.122
"It's nice and warm here," he thought.

39
00:02:46.423 --> 00:02:48.364
Swallow tucked his head under his wing.

40
00:02:51.226 --> 00:02:53.888
Nearby two women were talking loudly.

41
00:02:55.288 --> 00:02:59.251
"My gown for the king's ball is going to be beautiful!"

42
00:02:59.732 --> 00:03:00.192
one said.

43
00:03:00.212 --> 00:03:04.335
"But that lazy seamstress still hasn't finished it!"

44
00:03:04.355 --> 00:03:06.998
"Why not?"

45
00:03:07.478 --> 00:03:08.139
asked the other.

46
00:03:08.159 --> 00:03:11.381
"Something about her son.

47
00:03:11.701 --> 00:03:13.163
I think he has a cold."

48
00:03:16.165 --> 00:03:20.408
Swallow, who loved beautiful things, wished he could see this lovely gown.

49
00:03:20.428 --> 00:03:24.712
"But I must leave early in the morning," he thought.

50
00:03:25.728 --> 00:03:26.709
He closed his eyes.

51
00:03:28.569 --> 00:03:33.251
Plop! A drop of rain fell on his head, then another, and another.

52
00:03:33.271 --> 00:03:36.113
"Oh bother!"

53
00:03:36.133 --> 00:03:38.173
he grumbled.

54
00:03:38.193 --> 00:03:41.555
"This isn't a good place to sleep after all."

55
00:03:43.716 --> 00:03:44.856
Swallow flew upward.

56
00:03:45.977 --> 00:03:47.818
He expected to get soaking wet.

57
00:03:48.938 --> 00:03:50.519
But there were no clouds.

58
00:03:51.799 --> 00:03:52.780
And there was no rain.

59
00:03:54.664 --> 00:03:56.208
Swallow blinked in surprise.

60
00:03:57.511 --> 00:04:00.457
The water was coming from the statue!
